# CLOSURE (qa-pr1179-r9, quality-mgr): AC8's recursive rust_sources() scan
# test (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/observability.rs:99) independently
# confirmed closed by quality-mgr, arch-qa, and req-qa at 1d43815c6 -- all
# three separately traced every current call site of NullSqliteObservability
# in the crate and confirmed each is #[cfg(test)]-gated or the definition
# site itself. This finding's AC8 component is genuinely fixed.

# PARTIAL FIX + SEVERITY REASSESSMENT (qa-pr1179-r8, quality-mgr): AW.2
# round-8 (fee01b959) added
# ac8_null_sqlite_observability_is_test_only_in_the_source_contract
# (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/observability.rs:85), but it only does an
# include_str! substring match against observability.rs's own definition --
# it does not scan crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/ as the AC text requires,
# so it provides no regression protection against a future unguarded
# reference in any other file. Independently confirmed insufficient by
# quality-mgr, req-qa (filed as ATM-QA-AW2R8-002, Minor), and rust-qa-agent
# (filed as QA-001, Important) -- all three separately verified the current
# call sites (shared_db_reader_lanes.rs, writer/mod.rs, shared_db.rs,
# analyst_query.rs, lib.rs) are correctly #[cfg(test)]-gated today, so there
# is no live production violation, only a regression-detection gap.
# Severity downgraded from blocking to important to match this round's
# reviewer consensus (no live violation exists); team-lead may revise.
# Status remains open pending a real crate-wide source scan.

